  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 125 AM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nDry weather along with near normal temperatures will prevail for \ntoday through Wednesday as surface high pressure influences the \nregion. Meanwhile deeper moisture will begin to stream northward \nfrom the Texas panhandle into western Kansas for Wednesday into \nThursday as upper trough over over the western states migrates \nslowly east. Scattered to numerous showers/storms are expected to \ndevelop and stream north over western Kansas Wednesday-Thursday. \nSome of this activity will gradually spread eastward towards central \nKansas on Thursday and especially for Thursday night into Friday \nwith models showing upper wave pivoting east. Severe weather chances \nlook low this period with limited instability and weak wind shear \nanticipated. Models show the main upper level wave eventually \nejecting from the Rockies out into the central plains for Friday \nnight into Saturday. As a result, the weather pattern will remain \nunsettled with shower/storm chances continuing into Saturday across \ncentral/eastern Kansas.",
